#128 [architecture] sdd/solicitud-multi-libro-contacto/design (rev. 4 — FINAL, design-phase JD closed)
# Design: Multi-book solicitudes + contact/pickup fields

> Revision 4 is the FINAL design revision. Round 4 Judgment Day found 5 more issues, all narrower/mechanical than prior rounds (no CRITICALs, no data-integrity bugs) — the user explicitly decided to stop the design-review loop here (diminishing returns after 4 rounds) and carry these 5 items forward as explicit `sdd-tasks` requirements instead of further design-doc iteration. See "Deferred to sdd-tasks (Round 4 findings)" at the bottom — `sdd-tasks` MUST create a concrete task for each one; none may be silently dropped.

## Technical Approach
`solicitud_libros` junction as the accept/reject unit; `solicitudes` as header (contact/pickup once + legacy compat columns, documented via unconditional `sp_addextendedproperty`); `:id` rescoped to `solicitud_libros.id`; `aceptar()` transaction shape preserved verbatim, retargeted; `create()` as whole-transaction-retry with a batched (not looped) multi-row line insert, with explicit rowsAffected verification; additive-only migration with independently-guarded indexes and an independently-guarded, self-healing identity reseed. Staff list gates both action-button visibility AND dimming off a single `esPendiente` flag (no separate `esActiva`). TZ pin lives at the top of `app.js` (the module shared by the real server and every test) — placement wording needs one more precision pass, see deferred items.

## Architecture Decisions

| Topic | Choice | Alternatives rejected | Rationale |
|---|---|---|---|
| Accept/reject unit | `solicitud_libros.id` line | flip header estatus | Independent per-book resolution. |
| Header legacy cols | INSERT populates `libro_id`=first selected id, `estatus`='pendiente' literal; documented via unconditional `sp_addextendedproperty` (both `libro_id` and `estatus`) in the migration script | ALTER COLUMN to NULL; hedged/optional documentation | Zero constraint change; extended property makes staleness discoverable via `sys.extended_properties`/SSMS, not just app source. |
| Staff list mixed-status visibility | Query fetches all lines of any solicitud with ≥1 line matching the active filter | Per-line-only filtering (fragments a solicitud across filters) | User confirmed: show sibling lines with full context. |
| Staff list dimming/actionability | Single `esPendiente = (estatus === 'pendiente')` flag drives BOTH action-button visibility and (inverted) dimming — no separate `esActiva` | Two separate flags (`esActiva` for dimming, `esPendiente` for buttons) — created a dimmed-but-still-actionable visual contradiction | One flag, one meaning, no contradiction possible by construction. |
| Availability pre-check | one `WHERE id IN (@id0..@idN)` query, JS-resorted to match original submission order | N-loop; SQL ORDER BY via CASE | 1 round-trip; reused for confirmation list in correct order. |
| create() retry | whole-tx retry (begin→header OUTPUT id→batched multi-row line INSERT→commit; on 2627/2601 rollback+retry, <=5); line insert's `rowsAffected[0]` explicitly checked against `ids.length`, throws on mismatch | Looped per-book INSERTs (N round-trips); trusting the batch silently | Short transaction regardless of N; a dynamic-SQL row-count bug becomes loud, not silent. |
| `ids` null-filtering | `.filter(id => id !== null)` before dedup | Implicit/unstated null-handling | A `null` reaching the INSERT would produce an unhandled 500 instead of a clean 400. |
| Re-render status codes | input invalid → 400; state conflict → 409; tampered curp/nombre → 400 `error` | all-409 | Matches existing bad-nombre 400. |
| checkbox `checked` on re-render | controller precomputes `libros[].checked` | hbs helper | Keep views logic-free. |
| Date-only compare + TZ | `todayISO` via `getFullYear()/getMonth()/getDate()`; storage via `new Date(Date.UTC(y,m-1,d))` as `sql.Date`; **the comparison baseline is only correct because `process.env.TZ` is pinned to `'America/Mexico_City'` at the top of `src/app.js`** (fallback: `process.env.TZ \|\| 'America/Mexico_City'`), which both `src/index.js` (after its existing `dotenv.config()` call) and every test (`require('../src/app')` directly) load, so a `.env` override still works for the real server AND tests get a correct default without needing `.env` at all. Empirically confirmed on this project's actual Windows Node host that a runtime `process.env.TZ` mutation genuinely changes `Date` local-time interpretation (cross-timezone `getHours()` test, MX vs Tokyo, same fixed UTC instant, produced different — correct — results). **Exact insertion point relative to `app.js`'s existing `'use strict';` directive still needs a precision task — see deferred items.** | Pin in `index.js` only (doesn't cover tests); pin before `dotenv.config()` (breaks `.env` override); assume Windows honors runtime TZ mutation without checking (empirically verified instead) | The two entry points share exactly one common ancestor module (`app.js`) for the TZ pin to live in both places at once — but a third entry point (migration/DB scripts, which never require `app.js`) is NOT covered by this and needs its own explicit handling, see deferred items. |

## Staff list grouping — explicit pseudocode
```js
// rows: flat result of STAFF_LIST_QUERY, ORDER BY fecha_solicitud DESC, solicitud_id DESC, linea_id ASC
// (solicitud_id as an explicit second-level tiebreaker guarantees deterministic, contiguous grouping
// even when multiple solicitudes share an identical fecha_solicitud, e.g. a bulk historical backfill —
// verified: a plain JS Map keyed by solicitud_id is correct regardless of row contiguity/interleaving
// anyway, since it's a lookup-by-key structure, not a run-length grouping.)
function buildListContext(rows, estatusFiltro) {
  const bySolicitud = new Map();
  for (const row of rows) {
    if (!bySolicitud.has(row.solicitud_id)) {
      // Header fields are IDENTICAL across every row sharing one solicitud_id (same joined s.* columns) —
      // no "which occurrence wins" ambiguity; first-seen is simply the only occurrence that matters.
      bySolicitud.set(row.solicitud_id, {
        solicitud_id: row.solicitud_id, curp: row.curp, nombre_solicitante: row.nombre_solicitante,
        codigo_seguimiento: row.codigo_seguimiento, telefono: row.telefono, correo: row.correo,
        fecha_recoleccion_estimada: row.fecha_recoleccion_estimada, fecha_solicitud: row.fecha_solicitud,
        libros: [],
      });
    }
    const esPendiente = row.estatus === 'pendiente';
    bySolicitud.get(row.solicitud_id).libros.push({
      lineaId: row.linea_id, libro_titulo: row.libro_titulo, libro_folio: row.libro_folio,
      estatus: row.estatus, estatusLabel: ESTATUS_LABELS[row.estatus],
      badgeBlue: esPendiente, badgeGreen: row.estatus === 'aceptada', badgeRed: row.estatus === 'rechazada',
      esPendiente,
    });
  }
  return {
    solicitudes: [...bySolicitud.values()],
    estatusPendienteSelected: estatusFiltro === 'pendiente',
    estatusAceptadaSelected: estatusFiltro === 'aceptada',
    estatusRechazadaSelected: estatusFiltro === 'rechazada',
  };
}
```
Template: `{{#if this.esPendiente}}` action forms, `{{#unless this.esPendiente}}linea-atenuada{{/unless}}` dimming — same flag, two effects, no contradiction possible.

`estatus` query param whitelist: unchanged existing `normalizeEstatus`/`ESTATUS_VALUES = new Set(['pendiente','aceptada','rechazada'])` pattern already in `solicitudes.controller.js` today — falls back to `'pendiente'`, no new code pattern.

## SQL (exact)
```sql
-- STAFF_LIST_QUERY (fetches ALL lines of any solicitud with >=1 matching line, for sibling context)
SELECT sl.id AS linea_id, sl.estatus, sl.fecha_resolucion,
       s.id AS solicitud_id, s.curp, s.nombre_solicitante, s.codigo_seguimiento,
       s.fecha_solicitud, s.telefono, s.correo, s.fecha_recoleccion_estimada,
       l.titulo AS libro_titulo, l.folio AS libro_folio
FROM solicitud_libros sl
  INNER JOIN solicitudes s ON s.id = sl.solicitud_id
  INNER JOIN libros l ON l.id = sl.libro_id
WHERE sl.solicitud_id IN (
  SELECT DISTINCT solicitud_id FROM solicitud_libros WHERE estatus = @estatus
)
ORDER BY s.fecha_solicitud DESC, s.id DESC, sl.id ASC;

-- ACEPTAR_CHECK_QUERY (:id = solicitud_libros.id) — locking pattern verified sound by 2 independent
-- judges (reasoning-level; no live-DB run) across rounds 1-2; two different solicitud_libros.id rows
-- sharing one libro_id still serialize correctly via the shared UPDLOCK/HOLDLOCK on the libros row.
SELECT sl.estatus, sl.libro_id, l.copias_disponibles
FROM solicitud_libros sl WITH (UPDLOCK, HOLDLOCK)
  INNER JOIN libros l WITH (UPDLOCK, HOLDLOCK) ON l.id = sl.libro_id
WHERE sl.id = @id;
-- then UNCHANGED guarded UPDATE libros ... WHERE id=@libroId AND copias_disponibles>0 (rowsAffected re-checked),
-- then: UPDATE solicitud_libros SET estatus='aceptada', fecha_resolucion=GETDATE() WHERE id=@id;

-- rechazar (:id = solicitud_libros.id)
UPDATE solicitud_libros SET estatus='rechazada', fecha_resolucion=GETDATE()
WHERE id=@id AND estatus='pendiente';

-- tieneSolicitudPendiente (junction) — accepted pre-existing risk: unlocked SELECT outside any
-- transaction, same shape as production code today; a genuine double-submit race is not new here.
SELECT TOP 1 sl.id FROM solicitud_libros sl
  INNER JOIN solicitudes s ON s.id = sl.solicitud_id
WHERE s.curp=@curp AND sl.estatus='pendiente';

-- availability pre-check (+ confirmation source), JS-resorted by input order
SELECT id, titulo, folio FROM libros
WHERE id IN (@id0, @id1, ...) AND activo=1 AND copias_disponibles>0;
-- JS: const byId = new Map(avail.map(b => [b.id, b])); const ordered = ids.map(id => byId.get(id)).filter(Boolean);

-- header INSERT
INSERT INTO solicitudes (curp, nombre_solicitante, libro_id, estatus, codigo_seguimiento, telefono, correo, fecha_recoleccion_estimada)
OUTPUT INSERTED.id
VALUES (@curp, @nombre, @libroIdCompat, 'pendiente', @codigo, @telefono, @correo, @fecha);

-- line INSERT (batched multi-row, not looped)
INSERT INTO solicitud_libros (solicitud_id, libro_id) VALUES
  (@solicitudId, @libroId0), (@solicitudId, @libroId1), (@solicitudId, @libroId2);
```

## create() control flow
```
curp,nombre = strings(body); telRaw,correoRaw,fechaRaw = strings(body)
tel = telRaw.replace(/[\s-]/g,'')   // normalized value is what's stored, sql.VarChar(20)
ids = [].concat(body.libro_id ?? []).map(parseStrictInt).filter(id => id !== null)
ids = [...new Set(ids)]
if !CURP_REGEX(curp) || nombre blank || nombre>200 -> 400 render('error')
todayISO = localDateISO(new Date())   // correct given process.env.TZ pinned at app.js load
errs = validateContacto: TELEFONO_REGEX(/^\d{10}$/) on `tel`, CORREO_REGEX+len<=254, fecha real+>=todayISO
if errs || ids.length===0 || ids.length>30 -> libros=fetchLibrosDisponibles(); 400 render solicitud-libros(preserve tel/correo/fecha + seleccionados=ids + mensaje)
if tieneSolicitudPendiente(curp) -> 409 render solicitud-libros(preserve + pendiente mensaje)
avail = IN-check(ids); orderedAvail = ids.map(id => avail.find by id).filter(Boolean)
if orderedAvail.length !== ids.length -> 409 render solicitud-libros(preserve + no-disponible mensaje)
await poolConnect
for intento in 0..CODIGO_MAX_ATTEMPTS:
  codigo=generateCodigo(); tx=pool.transaction(); await tx.begin()
  try:
    h = tx.request().input('curp',sql.VarChar(18),curp).input('nombre',sql.VarChar(200),nombre)
         .input('libroIdCompat',sql.Int,ids[0]).input('codigo',sql.VarChar(10),codigo)
         .input('telefono',sql.VarChar(20),tel).input('correo',sql.VarChar(254),correo)
         .input('fecha',sql.Date,fechaUtcDate)
         .query(HEADER_INSERT)  // OUTPUT INSERTED.id
    solicitudId = h.recordset[0].id
    lineReq = tx.request().input('solicitudId', sql.Int, solicitudId)
    ids.forEach((libroId, i) => lineReq.input(`libroId${i}`, sql.Int, libroId))
    lineResult = await lineReq.query(buildBatchedLineInsertSql(ids.length))
    if lineResult.rowsAffected[0] !== ids.length:
      throw new Error(`Expected to insert ${ids.length} solicitud_libros rows, affected ${lineResult.rowsAffected[0]}`)
    await tx.commit()
    return render solicitud-confirmacion { codigo, libros: orderedAvail.map(b=>({titulo,folio})) }
  catch err:
    try{ await tx.rollback() }catch(rb){ console.error('Rollback failed:', rb) }
    if DUPLICATE_CODE_ERROR_NUMBERS.has(err.number) continue
    throw err
throw new Error('No se pudo generar un código de seguimiento único.')
```
New constants: `TELEFONO_MAX_LENGTH=20, CORREO_MAX_LENGTH=254, MAX_LIBROS_POR_SOLICITUD=30, TELEFONO_REGEX, CORREO_REGEX, FECHA_REGEX`.

**Accepted risks, not fixed (explicitly, not by oversight):** rollback-failure-then-retry connection-pool release behavior unverified against real mssql/tedious semantics; unlocked `tieneSolicitudPendiente` double-submit race is pre-existing, not introduced by this change; backfill `NOT EXISTS` anti-join re-scan cost at scale; `GET /solicitudes` has no pagination (pre-existing, and this change increases rows-per-solicitud).

## Migration DDL (scripts/migrate-solicitud-multi-libro.js; npm `migrate:solicitud-multi-libro`)
```sql
IF OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitud_libros','U') IS NULL
BEGIN
 CREATE TABLE dbo.solicitud_libros(
  id INT IDENTITY(1,1) CONSTRAINT PK_solicitud_libros PRIMARY KEY,
  solicitud_id INT NOT NULL, libro_id INT NOT NULL,
  estatus VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL CONSTRAINT DF_solicitud_libros_estatus DEFAULT 'pendiente'
    CONSTRAINT CK_solicitud_libros_estatus CHECK (estatus IN ('pendiente','aceptada','rechazada')),
  fecha_resolucion DATETIME NULL,
  CONSTRAINT FK_sl_solicitud FOREIGN KEY(solicitud_id) REFERENCES dbo.solicitudes(id),
  CONSTRAINT FK_sl_libro FOREIGN KEY(libro_id) REFERENCES dbo.libros(id),
  CONSTRAINT UQ_solicitud_libros_solicitud_libro UNIQUE (solicitud_id, libro_id));
END
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.indexes WHERE name = 'IX_sl_solicitud' AND object_id = OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitud_libros'))
  CREATE INDEX IX_sl_solicitud ON dbo.solicitud_libros(solicitud_id);
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.indexes WHERE name = 'IX_sl_estatus' AND object_id = OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitud_libros'))
  CREATE INDEX IX_sl_estatus ON dbo.solicitud_libros(estatus);

-- Identity reseed: independent, self-healing check (NOT bundled with CREATE TABLE) — re-evaluated on
-- every script run so a prior partial run that created the table without reseeding self-corrects.
-- This is a one-time feature-rollout step; @safeSeed is recomputed from the live watermark each run,
-- which is harmless (never shrinks) but pointless to re-run routinely — state this in the script's
-- own --help/header comment.
IF OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitud_libros','U') IS NOT NULL
BEGIN
  DECLARE @maxSolicitudId INT = (SELECT ISNULL(MAX(id), 0) FROM dbo.solicitudes);
  DECLARE @safeSeed INT = @maxSolicitudId + 10000;
  DECLARE @currentIdent INT = ISNULL(IDENT_CURRENT('dbo.solicitud_libros'), 0);
  IF @currentIdent < @safeSeed
    EXEC('DBCC CHECKIDENT (''dbo.solicitud_libros'', RESEED, ' + CAST(@safeSeed AS VARCHAR(20)) + ')');
END

-- Legacy-column documentation: unconditional (not hedged), independently guarded.
-- NOTE (deferred to sdd-tasks, Round 4): the `class = 1` guard below is necessary but not sufficient —
-- class=1 (OBJECT_OR_COLUMN) matches BOTH table-level (minor_id=0) and column-level (minor_id=column_id)
-- extended properties; the guard must ALSO filter minor_id to the actual column_id to be airtight.
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.extended_properties WHERE major_id=OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitudes')
    AND minor_id=(SELECT column_id FROM sys.columns WHERE object_id=OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitudes') AND name='libro_id')
    AND name='MS_Description' AND class=1 /* AND minor_id filter already present above via the subquery */)
  EXEC sp_addextendedproperty @name=N'MS_Description',
    @value=N'Legacy compatibility placeholder frozen at solicitud creation time (first selected book). NOT authoritative after creation — join through solicitud_libros for true per-book status.',
    @level0type=N'SCHEMA', @level0name=N'dbo', @level1type=N'TABLE', @level1name=N'solicitudes', @level2type=N'COLUMN', @level2name=N'libro_id';
IF NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM sys.extended_properties WHERE major_id=OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitudes')
    AND minor_id=(SELECT column_id FROM sys.columns WHERE object_id=OBJECT_ID('dbo.solicitudes') AND name='estatus')
    AND name='MS_Description' AND class=1)
  EXEC sp_addextendedproperty @name=N'MS_Description',
    @value=N'Legacy compatibility placeholder, always ''pendiente'' after solicitud creation. NOT authoritative after creation — join through solicitud_libros for true per-book status.',
    @level0type=N'SCHEMA', @level0name=N'dbo', @level1type=N'TABLE', @level1name=N'solicitudes', @level2type=N'COLUMN', @level2name=N'estatus';

IF NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='dbo' AND TABLE_NAME='solicitudes' AND COLUMN_NAME='telefono') ALTER TABLE dbo.solicitudes ADD telefono VARCHAR(20) NULL;
IF NOT EXISTS(... TABLE_SCHEMA='dbo' AND TABLE_NAME='solicitudes' AND COLUMN_NAME='correo') ALTER TABLE dbo.solicitudes ADD correo VARCHAR(254) NULL;
IF NOT EXISTS(... TABLE_SCHEMA='dbo' AND TABLE_NAME='solicitudes' AND COLUMN_NAME='fecha_recoleccion_estimada') ALTER TABLE dbo.solicitudes ADD fecha_recoleccion_estimada DATE NULL;
INSERT INTO dbo.solicitud_libros(solicitud_id,libro_id,estatus,fecha_resolucion)
SELECT s.id,s.libro_id,s.estatus,s.fecha_resolucion FROM dbo.solicitudes s
WHERE s.libro_id IS NOT NULL AND NOT EXISTS(SELECT 1 FROM dbo.solicitud_libros sl WHERE sl.solicitud_id=s.id);
SELECT COLUMN_NAME,IS_NULLABLE,DATA_TYPE,CHARACTER_MAXIMUM_LENGTH FROM INFORMATION_SCHEMA.COLUMNS
WHERE TABLE_SCHEMA='dbo' AND TABLE_NAME='solicitudes' AND COLUMN_NAME IN ('libro_id','estatus','fecha_resolucion');
```
`--dry-run`: existence checks + nullability report only; no CREATE/ALTER/backfill/reseed/extended-property writes.

**NOTE (deferred to sdd-tasks, Round 4):** this migration script is itself an entry point that does NOT go through `app.js` (it follows `scripts/import-libros.js`'s pattern: `require('dotenv').config()` + `require('../src/db')` directly) — so the `app.js` TZ pin does NOT cover it. If the script computes/backfills any date-sensitive values, it needs its own explicit TZ handling; `sdd-tasks` must decide and implement this (likely: the same `process.env.TZ` fallback line, duplicated at the top of the migration script itself, OR extracted to a tiny shared module both `app.js` and every DB script require first).

## View data contracts (res.render shapes)
- `solicitud-libros`: `{ curp, nombre, telefono, correo, fecha, mensaje, libros:[{id,titulo,folio,autor,genero,copias_disponibles,checked:bool}] }`. Checkboxes `name="libro_id[]"`, `{{#if this.checked}}checked{{/if}}`. Client-side "at least one" UX check is a nice-to-have alongside the server-side `ids.length===0` guard.
- `solicitud-confirmacion`: `{ codigo, libros:[{titulo,folio}] }` — original selection order.
- `solicitudes` (staff, grouped): `{ estatus*Selected, mensaje, solicitudes:[{ solicitud_id,curp,nombre_solicitante,codigo_seguimiento,telefono,correo,fecha_recoleccion_estimada,fecha_solicitud, libros:[{ lineaId,libro_titulo,libro_folio,estatus,estatusLabel,badgeBlue,badgeGreen,badgeRed,esPendiente }] }] }`. Single `esPendiente` flag gates both action forms and dimming.
- Known scaling note (accepted risk): `GET /solicitudes` has no pagination; this change increases rows-per-solicitud.

## mockPool extension (test/helpers/mockPool.js)
- `insertedId` option: `OUTPUT INSERTED.id`-matching SQL returns `{ recordset:[{id:insertedId}], rowsAffected:[1] }`.
- `sequence` option on `createFakeRequest`/`createFakeTransaction`: the call-counter lives on the **transaction mock's closure**, shared across every `.request()` call that transaction instance produces (confirmed: `create()`'s transaction body issues exactly 2 query calls per attempt — header, then batched lines — with nothing else in between; pre-checks run on plain `pool.request()` before the transaction even opens, so they never touch this counter).
- Line-insert `rowsAffected` reflects the actual VALUES-tuple count parsed from the INSERT SQL text (not hardcoded `1`), so a test can assert what happens on both a correct count and a deliberately-wrong one — makes `create()`'s new rowsAffected-mismatch check actually testable. Falls back to `1` for any non-multi-VALUES INSERT (backward compatible).
- Whole-tx retry-then-succeed: test-level `pool.transaction` call-counter closure (no `mockPool.js` change needed), same pattern as the existing "racing accepts" test.
- Retargeted concurrency test: two DIFFERENT `solicitud_libros.id` values sharing one `libro_id`.
- **Residual (deferred, low priority):** no direct unit test of `buildListContext`'s grouping algorithm itself (N rows/M solicitudes → M correctly-grouped entries) exists yet — only an integration-level dimming assertion. A Map-keying regression could theoretically slip through if it doesn't also manifest as a dimming bug.

## File Changes
| File | Action | Description |
|---|---|---|
| scripts/migrate-solicitud-multi-libro.js | Create | Idempotent DDL: per-object guards, self-healing identity reseed, unconditional extended-property documentation (with correct minor_id-based class-1 guard), backfill, nullability report; own TZ handling per deferred item below |
| package.json | Modify | Add `migrate:solicitud-multi-libro` script |
| src/index.js | No change (already `dotenv.config()` first, then `require('./app')`) | |
| src/app.js | Modify | TZ pin — exact insertion point (relative to existing `'use strict';`) is a deferred precision task, see below |
| .env.example | Modify | Document optional `TZ` override |
| src/controllers/solicitudes.controller.js | Modify | Grouped staff list (`esPendiente`-only), transactional multi-insert create w/ rowsAffected verification, junction accept/reject/pending, contact validation, estatus-param whitelist |
| src/routes/solicitudes.routes.js | No change | URL shapes identical |
| src/views/solicitud-libros.hbs | Modify | checkboxes + 3 fields + value/checked preservation |
| src/views/solicitud-confirmacion.hbs | Modify | list requested books, original order |
| src/views/solicitudes.hbs | Modify | group by solicitud w/ dimmed sibling lines; single `esPendiente`-gated actions |
| test/helpers/mockPool.js | Modify | OUTPUT INSERTED.id + shared-counter `sequence` + VALUES-tuple-aware rowsAffected |
| test/solicitudes.routes.test.js | Modify | rewrite assertions; junction + tx-create branches; retry-then-succeed; header-succeeds-line-fails; rowsAffected-mismatch; two-different-lines-same-book race; esPendiente button-gating/dimming test |

## Testing Strategy
| Layer | What | How |
|---|---|---|
| Unit | contact/N validation, TZ-safe date compare, telefono normalize, null-filtering, **(deferred) a direct test that the TZ pin mechanism itself works, not just its downstream date-comparison outcome** | direct + 400 re-render assertions |
| Integration | create tx multi-insert (batched + rowsAffected check), whole-tx retry-then-succeed, header-succeeds-line-fails rollback, per-line accept/reject, junction pending block, grouped staff list w/ sibling dimming AND correct `esPendiente`-only button gating, availability IN-check w/ order preservation, **(deferred) direct unit test of `buildListContext` grouping** | supertest + dual mock, concurrency-race test w/ two different lines sharing one book |
| Migration | idempotency (re-run no-op incl. per-object guards AND the self-healing reseed check), --dry-run no writes, backfill NOT EXISTS, extended properties present with correct minor_id filter | manual/script dry-run against DB (out of unit suite) |

## Migration / Rollout
Additive. Run `npm run migrate:solicitud-multi-libro -- --dry-run` first, then live. Rollback: `DROP TABLE solicitud_libros`, drop 3 columns, drop extended properties, revert code (incl. TZ pin); legacy single-book path fully restorable.

## Deferred to sdd-tasks (Round 4 findings — design-phase JD closed by user decision, none may be silently dropped)
1. **TZ pin exact placement**: insert `process.env.TZ = process.env.TZ || 'America/Mexico_City';` immediately AFTER the existing `'use strict';` directive at the top of `src/app.js`, NOT literally as line 1 — inserting it before `'use strict'` would silently disable strict mode for the whole file (verified against the real current file, which begins with `'use strict';` then `const path = require('node:path');`).
2. **TZ mechanism regression test**: add a permanent automated test that verifies the TZ *pin itself* takes effect (e.g., set `process.env.TZ` to something else, clear `require.cache` for `app.js`, re-require it, assert `process.env.TZ === 'America/Mexico_City'` or that a cross-timezone date comparison changes as expected) — not just a downstream "pickup date submitted this evening" assertion that could false-positive on a CI host whose default TZ already happens to coincide.
3. **Extended-property guard correctness**: the `class = 1` filter alone doesn't distinguish column-level from table-level extended properties (class 1 = OBJECT_OR_COLUMN, covers both); the guard must also filter on the actual `minor_id` (already done via the `minor_id=(SELECT column_id ...)` subquery in the SQL above — `sdd-tasks` must implement it exactly as shown, not simplify it back to a bare `class=1` check).
